{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-b-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:09:56.627Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d1188513b61c91ef21fa48fb30ace887bf2c27183a266130aeed208d504ef01b","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Moss's notes have two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: at the Eau Claire yard, drivers checking in by tablet for the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their bay-assignment texts. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next 04:00 shift got through the gate without help.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went up to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date, so I can't tell when that was.\n\nThings to know before you paste these in:\n- #4419 doesn't have the \"PD-\" prefix the other one has. I've copied both exactly as Moss wrote them.\n- Moss's 14 Sep 2025 North digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal note both mention Quarrendon but have no ticket numbers.\n- Moss's 2 Jan 2026 Central digest has tickets #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Marrow Fieldworks, so I left them out.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company that isn't a customer, so I left it out too.\n\nI only looked through Moss's shared files, not channel messages. I can also check #north-team or #inc-qfl-sev1 for tickets if you'd like."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
